                {
                  "phase": "grammar",
                  "type": "grammar_rule",
                  "content": {
                    "title": "wish and if only",
                    "explanation": "Wish expresa que algo fuera distinto. El tiempo verbal da un paso atrás:\n• wish + past simple: una situación presente que nos gustaría cambiar: I wish I had more time.\n• wish + could: una habilidad que no tenemos: I wish I could cook like him.\n• wish + would: un hábito de otra persona que nos molesta: I wish he wouldn't cook at two a.m. (no se usa con I).\n• wish + past perfect: arrepentimiento por el pasado: I wish I'd known earlier.\n\nIf only funciona igual, pero es más enfático: If only all problems were this easy.",
                    "table": {
                      "headers": [
                        "Estructura",
                        "Para",
                        "Ejemplo"
                      ],
                      "rows": [
                        [
                          "wish + pasado",
                          "situación presente que te gustaría cambiar",
                          "I wish I had more time."
                        ],
                        [
                          "wish + could",
                          "habilidad que no tienes",
                          "I wish I could cook like him."
                        ],
                        [
                          "wish + would",
                          "hábitos molestos de otros",
                          "I wish he wouldn't cook at two a.m."
                        ],
                        [
                          "wish + past perfect",
                          "arrepentimiento del pasado",
                          "I wish I'd known earlier."
                        ],
                        [
                          "if only",
                          "igual, pero más enfático",
                          "If only all problems were this easy."
                        ]
                      ]
                    },
                    "examples": [
                      "I wish Ollie wouldn't cook at two in the morning.",
                      "I wish I could cook like him.",
                      "I wish I'd known earlier!",
                      "If only all problems were this easy."
                    ]
                  }
